==English==

===Etymology===
1670s, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|subtrahendus|lang=la}} {{term|numerus||number to be subtracted|lang=la}}, form of {{term|subtrahō||I pull out from under, I subtract|lang=la}} (English {{term|subtract|lang=en}}).<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Surface analysis is {{suffix|subtract|end|t2=patient (recipient) of action|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsʌbtrəhɛnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|arithmetic|lang=en}} A number or quantity to be subtracted from another.
#: ''In the subtraction 10 &minus; 4, 4 is the subtrahend.''

